{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>נדחף.</b> By himself, and he was mourning. חפוי ראש is a noun [lit. one whose head is covered]; the sense is, covering his head. The witness is ופני המן חפו, and it is from the same root as ויחפהו, if it is in a different binyan."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The comment parses חפוי ראש (Esther 6:12) and cross-references ופני המן חפו (Esther 7:8) and ויחפהו (II Sam 15:30). פעול read as a noun pattern; rendered accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:12.334239938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}